Perhaps it is the static typer in me, but I would go so far as to say that it 
does not make sense for a place in a gismu to be able to be an abstraction or a 
concrete object. Objects filling a given predicate place have to fulfill certain 
basic, fundamental requirements to make semantic sense, and I think this is one 
of them. To me, even though I use "want" in this way in English, a {se djica} 
being a concrete object is like adding a function to a number.


mu'o mi'e latros.
